tract requirement intended to be encoded in the executable rule beyond the request trigger?\"],\"question_relation\":{\"evidence\":[{\"span_ids\":[\"span.87fe9b4d756ce4f6b8af2de3533899141aeec92bc718b9175661655fc985b7bd\"]},{\"span_ids\":[\"span.7b77852002e4dd7c23d837a964fc24681baa34735da2edc7521e129843ce817b\"]}],\"question_hash\":\"0b59742c020d7fae2612f418b62d0f6d929bff0b42768c9c24d1d829a8f0c9c9\",\"rationale\":\"Paragraph 14 expressly conditions demonstration on an SFC request, while footnote 5 states confirmation and demonstration content without repeating the request phrase. These passages directly bear on whether the request activates the duty and on the unresolved relationship between trigger and content.\",\"status\":\"RELEVANT\"},\"source_support\":{\"evidence\":[{\"span_ids\":[\"span.87fe9b4d756ce4f6b8af2de3533899141aeec92bc718b9175661655fc985b7bd\"]},{\"span_ids\":[\"span.7b77852002e4dd7c23d837a964fc24681baa34735da2edc7521e129843ce817b\"]}],\"rationale\":\"Paragraph 14 supports a request-conditioned obligation to demonstrate management and operational soundness, ownership record keeping and smart-contract integrity to the SFC's satisfaction. Footnote 5 supports minimum content tied to paragraphs 10 to 13 and high-confidence absence of smart-contract vulnerabilities. The source does not establish that a request was actually made or that demonstration occurred.\",\"status\":\"SUPPORTED\"}}]}"}}
